  "narrative": "No new independent validation estimates or response deadlines were delivered, assessments_due is empty, and the voluntary validation request budget is exhausted; I therefore make no claim-status changes. Using the already signed convention, positive signed estimates for direction +1 claims mean exposed-minus-comparator raw differences in higher dependency_composite, i.e. less negative composite scores and weaker measured dependency, while positive signed estimates for direction -1 claims mean raw lower composite scores and stronger measured dependency. The principal supported supplied-dataset associations are KEAP1 loss, SMARCA4 loss, TP53 loss, MSI-high status, and PTEN loss. KEAP1 loss has the strongest accepted positive composite association, with signed discovery estimate about +0.83 units and independent validation about +0.85 units, implying higher raw composite and weaker measured dependency. SMARCA4 loss has a strong accepted inverse raw association, with signed discovery and validation estimates about +0.80 to +0.83, implying lower raw composite and stronger measured dependency. TP53 loss, after the registered direction correction, is associated with moderately higher raw composite and weaker measured dependency, signed discovery and validation estimates about +0.42. MSI-high status is associated with lower raw composite and stronger measured dependency, signed estimate about +0.79, and remains internally robust across many adequately powered contexts including adenocarcinoma, TP53-intact lines, media-serum strata, MYC-high and MYC-low contexts, age >=65, Avana-library lines, and screen-quality strata, although it was not independently validated within this run because the validation budget was exhausted. PTEN loss is supported as a moderate inverse raw association with lower composite and stronger dependency, discovery signed estimate about +0.227 and validation about +0.279, with multiple supportive context estimates whose lower bounds clear the 0.15-unit threshold; PTEN localization in TP53/SMARCA4-intact lines is reasonably clear, while the TP53/KEAP1/SMARCA4/STK11 wild-type boundary estimate +0.231 has a lower bound slightly below threshold and should be read as supportive boundary localization rather than a standalone robust context claim. Accepted context checks for KEAP1, SMARCA4, and TP53 in screen_roc_auc >=0.95, and for MSI-high in age >=65 and Avana-library lines, strengthen internal compatibility but do not establish causality, mechanism, or external generalizability. Negative findings are broad and important: constructed research markers D, E, and F are null; MTAP, ARID1A, STK11, KRAS, PIK3CA, NF1, BRCA2, APC, SMAD4, EGFR amplification, ERBB2 amplification, MYC amplification, RB1, and sex are null or subthreshold in main tests; most technical availability, batch, and library indicators are null or small; and research-signature main-effect exact-bin comparisons failed with empty cells and support no scientific claim. Most interaction or effect-modification tests are negative, opposite, or too imprecise, including tests involving lineage subtype, screen batch, media serum, MYC expression, EMT, hypoxia, stemness, IFN-gamma, growth rate, age, sex, co-alteration patterns, and many co-registered interactions; these indicate lack of evidence for those modifiers in this dataset, not proof of absence. The main unresolved area is CDKN2A loss, whose broad signed estimate is near threshold at about +0.141 with interval below and above the 0.15 boundary, and whose copy-number and context-specific tests remain imprecise or below threshold; CDKN2A should not be accepted as a scientifically meaningful dependency association in this supplied dataset. A secondary unresolved area is precise PTEN localization, where some context point estimates are supportive but several age or co-alteration strata are underpowered. The most informative next step is prespecified independent external validation of the five core associations, especially MSI-high status if only internal evidence is available. If additional supplied-dataset analyses are possible, they should use a small theory-led, adequately powered set of broad strata or continuous copy-number/phenotype models, particularly for CDKN2A and PTEN, rather than many post hoc small co-alteration strata. All conclusions remain descriptive associations in this supplied dataset for a composite dependency endpoint, not causal effects, not single-gene knockout measurements, and not claims of generalizability.",
  "research_notes": "Iteration 23 final synthesis: no new validation and no response deadlines; validation budget exhausted. Retain KEAP1 loss (higher raw composite, weaker dependency), SMARCA4 loss (lower raw composite, stronger dependency), TP53 loss (higher raw composite, weaker dependency), MSI-high status (lower raw composite, stronger dependency), and PTEN loss (lower raw composite, stronger dependency) as principal supplied-dataset associations. KEAP1, SMARCA4, TP53, and PTEN include independent validation; MSI-high is internally robust but not independently validated in-run. CDKN2A remains unresolved near-threshold and should not be accepted. Research-signature main-effect bin tests are invalid; no claims. Null or unsupported findings include research markers D/E/F, most secondary alterations, technical covariates, and most interaction/effect-modification tests. PTEN boundary localizations require caution. Next best analysis: prespecified external validation of the five core associations, especially MSI-high; internally, only a small adequately powered theory-led set for CDKN2A and PTEN localization using broad or continuous copy-number models, avoiding many tiny post hoc co-alteration strata. Maintain scope: descriptive composite-endpoint associations, not causal, not single-gene knockout, not generalizable."
}
